1785724339968451	console-w-qw	itc:v3:AWKfJMzJnJnnxAAAAAAAQb6ttbre-AAAAAEuCA		item.assign	bn-305	{"action":"assign","agent":"console-w-qw"}	blake3:ppWD9-A4ScfakGXS0WM9O8m-a4K546kXxGFtALaN5LQ
1785724452626455	console-w-qw	itc:v3:AWKfJMzJnJnnxAAAAAAAQb6ttbre-AAAAAEuCQ		item.comment	bn-305	{"body":"Done in workspace bn-305. Verdict: KEEP the assertion -- it documents a real (if soft) authoring convention, not an accident. Investigation: nothing in console-core's engine treats sprite index 0 specially (gfx.rs's spr() just does base_x/base_y = (n%16, n//16)*8 for any n, no special-casing of 0), so it is NOT an engine invariant. It's a cart-authoring convention: color 0 is already spr()'s transparent color (SPEC.md Palette section), so an all-zero sprite 0 is a natural by-construction no-op/placeholder tile id. demo.cart's own gfx_meta confirms the convention in practice -- every declared sprite (player/star/gem/moth) starts at tile 1 or later, leaving tile 0 deliberately unused. This matches the common PICO-8-style convention of reserving sprite 0 as the empty tile. Changes: added an explanatory comment above the assertion in crates/console-core/tests/cart_parse.rs (demo_cart_parses) covering this reasoning, and added a line to skills/build-cart/SKILL.md's sprite-authoring section: 'Leave tile 0 blank -- sprite 0 is reserved as the empty tile by convention ... nothing in the engine enforces this, but the demo cart follows it and its test suite checks for it.' Diff scoped to exactly those two files (no other console-core changes) since another worker is concurrently editing console-core audio+gfx. cargo test --workspace green (no test count change, cart_parse.rs still 7 passed)."}	blake3:49LBy1fH7ykTNrshr-sOKGeync9zWS92zyfI2LxZ61M
