1785724578630919	console-w-372	itc:v3:AWKSeZyZnJmZ5EAAAAAAQavbrbrbegAAAAEwAw		item.comment	bn-372	{"body":"Done in .maw/workspaces/bn-372 (commit 5a388d5), ready for the lead to merge.\n\nHEADLINE: goldens did NOT change. MIX_GAIN stays at 1/4, so DEMO_AUDIO_GOLDEN (0xbc2bd5e1f8c7f31e) and SOUNDTEST_GROOVE_GOLDEN (0x993ee5118be1bec4) both still pass untouched, and web/smoke.cjs's AUDIO_GOLDEN is still valid against the committed wasm engine. No golden re-recording, no smoke.cjs edit.\n\nHeadroom analysis (new mix_headroom_* tests in crates/console-core/tests/audio.rs):\n- 4 full-scale voices in phase -> exactly 1.0 (unchanged worst case)\n- 6 full-scale voices in phase -> 1.5, hard-clipped by the final clamp (~1/3 of samples pinned). Documented as an authoring constraint, not fixed: rescaling to 1/6 would move every golden and make every 4-voice cart a third quieter.\n- any non-zero master drive bounds output below full scale (MAKEUP[d] < 1) so it never reaches the clamp -- a free limiter. 6 voices at vol 4 peak at 0.857.\n- demo.cart peaks at 0.32, soundtest groove at ~0.21: real content has plenty of room.\n\nAllocation: sfx(n) auto-picks the lowest channel owned by neither music nor sfx; steal target is now ch5; sfx(n,ch)/sfx(-1,ch) take 0-5 and the error message says 'expected 0-5'.\n\nPatterns: 'pat <id> [...] : ch0 ch1 ch2 ch3 [ch4 ch5]' accepts 4-6 slots, omitted trailing slots silent, existing 4-slot carts parse identically. Parsing lives in audio.rs, not cart.rs -- cart.rs needed no change.\n\nFiles: crates/console-core/src/audio.rs, crates/console-core/tests/audio.rs, crates/console-agent/tests/audio.rs (channels.len() 4->6), SPEC.md, skills/build-cart/SKILL.md. api.rs untouched (validation is in lua_sfx). Carts untouched.\n\nTests: cargo test --workspace all green (core audio 78 -> 86). cargo clippy --all-targets clean.\n\nINTEGRATION NOTE FOR THE LEAD: the committed web/engine.js is still a 4-channel build. Existing content plays identically so the smoke test passes as-is, but carts that use ch4/ch5 or 5-/6-slot patterns will NOT work in packed HTML until engine.js is rebuilt (web/build-engine.sh). Recommend a rebuild before any cart starts using the new channels."}	blake3:CzJqb_nyfKvlfyoD6Xwy4_crJQz_WyxvGSKj7cPU7nQ
1785724615073421	console-dev	itc:v3:AWLmTP-ZOTJklAAAAAAAQe1v-11rVAAAAAEuVg		item.move	bn-372	{"state":"done"}	blake3:cm6AU-Ci3djlaAT-ATo0DiDzd9N0HQS5PHJEbdFU3Eg
1785724884773405	console-w-cp0	itc:v3:AWLOTk_JkkknMkQAAAAAQd11-tVV2oAAAAEyAw		item.comment	bn-cp0	{"body":"Draw-state pass landed in workspace bn-cp0 (commit 2a44bd1) — NOT merged, lead merges.\n\nImplemented in console-core: new gfx::DrawState (camera offset, inclusive screen-space clip rect clamped to screen, draw palette, display palette, palt mask) threaded through every primitive; new Lua globals camera()/clip()/pal()/palt(). Console::display_palette() + draw_state(). Framebuffer stays raw draw-space indices.\n\nDesign calls:\n* cls RESPECTS the clip rect (modern-PICO-8 windowed clear), ignores camera and draw palette. Documented in SPEC.\n* palt is tested on the sprite's SOURCE colour BEFORE the draw palette remaps it, so pal(1,0) draws colour-1 pixels as 0 rather than hiding them.\n* Draw state persists across frames — nothing auto-resets it.\n* pal() with no args resets both maps AND palt.\n* Empty/negative/off-screen clip rects collapse to a draws-nothing rect (no wraparound).\n\nPlumbing: console-agent encode_png(fb, dpal) + screenshot_png applies it (screen_text stays raw); console-web con_dpal() -> *const u8 (16 bytes, no handle arg — this ABI has no handle concept) added to EXPORTED_FUNCTIONS; web/template.html rebuilds a 16-entry RGBA lut per frame and blits palette[dpal[idx]], feature-detecting _con_dpal so older engines degrade to identity.\n\nVerification: cargo test --workspace all green (19 suites, incl. 24 new tests in crates/console-core/tests/draw_state.rs + 2 console-agent unit tests). clippy clean. web/engine.js REBUILT; node web/smoke.cjs PASS (0 failures) with fb golden 0x5e743aea and audio golden 0xbc2bd5e1f8c7f31e unchanged. Verified end-to-end that an agent screenshot shows the fade while screen_text is byte-identical.\n\nLead note: web/engine.js is rebuilt in this workspace, so any packed dist needs a repack after merge. I reverted rustfmt-version churn on files I did not touch (audio.rs, sprite/*, agent tests) to keep the diff conflict-free — the local rustfmt is newer than the one the repo was formatted with, so avoid a blanket 'cargo fmt --all' at merge time."}	blake3:W7YKVPn82UrzOhX4dUQ0CRQoZCtLHe5Y92W_vIfw5-Y
1785725076721883	console-dev	itc:v3:AWLmTP-ZOTJklAAAAAAAQe1v-11rVAAAAAEuVw		item.move	bn-cp0	{"state":"done"}	blake3:oLBbYmEm4aQD4eUd3LOZ7XxUvyR7UvinmdY505W8m-o
