1785725657174024	console-w-qw2	itc:v3:AWLJJyZk5JmSeZQAAAAAQdV1tdW1e0AAAAEyAw		item.comment	bn-3gj	{"body":"Implemented sprite dump/poke in workspace bn-3gj (top request from demo-art friction report). dump: console-agent sprite dump <cart> <target> [--frame N] prints a '#' coordinate header + hex rows. poke: console-agent sprite poke <cart> <target> [--frame N] (--rows a,b,... | --stdin) [--dry-run] writes rows back via the same atomic rewrite path sprite edit uses; --stdin skips '#' lines so dump | poke --stdin round-trips directly. Frame resolution matches sprite edit (raw sheet frame index), factored into shared sprite::resolve_rect. RPC untouched by design: rpc.rs only mirrors view commands (render/strip/onion/diff/ghost/lint), no edit-side RPC exists to extend. SKILL.md updated with dump/poke lines + workflow note. Tests: 18 new tests in tests/sprite_poke.rs covering basic writes, selective row rewrite, --frame, --dry-run, error paths (bad hex/row length/row count/unknown target/missing source/both sources), and round-trip guarantees (dump-then-poke no-op, poke-then-dump equality, plus a real subprocess dump|poke pipe). cargo test --workspace green (all suites pass). Committed at 19b30b8. Not merged — awaiting lead."}	blake3:oopXhQI-LY2H6TpQzDIGdgKI9aSIbXKOrJu_I6WTwh0
1785725662105002	console-w-qw2	itc:v3:AWLJJyZk5JmSeZQAAAAAQdV1tdW1e0AAAAEyBA		item.move	bn-2r6	{"state":"doing"}	blake3:lC3CS6Dx0FwWBtUcaIPCGA2pZWvDh9zFKpRUCftEf6g
1785725662119966	console-w-qw2	itc:v3:AWLJJyZk5JmSeZQAAAAAQdV1tdW1e0AAAAEyBQ		item.assign	bn-2r6	{"action":"assign","agent":"console-w-qw2"}	blake3:wuecxzUOebROFTcKb77tGBJG7B_URGrUjSbouAu58jY
1785725811188160	console-w-153	itc:v3:AWKSSZJJ5Myf80AAAAAAQaq1V62v-wAAAAEwAw		item.comment	bn-153	{"body":"Tile map runtime landed in workspace bn-153 (commit 456fcf0). NOT merged — lead merges.\n\nFORMAT: __map__ = rows of tile ids, 2 hex chars per cell (00-ff), fixed 128x64 cells (8192 bytes). Same conventions as __sprites__: # comment lines, blank lines skipped, short rows pad with tile 0, missing rows tile 0. Unlike __sprites__ it REJECTS instead of truncating — overlong row, odd-length row, >64 rows, non-hex digit all give Error::Cart naming the section-relative line (losing terrain silently is worse than failing to load). Tile 0 = empty cell, skipped per-cell before any pixel is read.\n\nAPI: map([cel_x],[cel_y],[sx],[sy],[cel_w],[cel_h]) with PICO-8 defaults (bare map() = whole map at 0,0); mget(cx,cy) -> id, 0 off-map; mset(cx,cy,[v]) no-op off-map, v masked to 0-255. Out-of-range cels skipped, no wrap, no error.\n\nREUSES spr(): spr()'s inner loop is extracted into a private gfx::blit(); spr() and map() both call it, so camera/clip/pal/palt apply to map cells by construction rather than by duplicated logic. Pinned by a test asserting map() and the equivalent spr() calls give byte-identical framebuffers under 8 different draw states. No allocation in the draw path; per-tile-row and per-tile clip rejects. Measured: full-screen scrolling map + print = ~11us/frame (0.07% of the 16.6ms budget).\n\nSTATE: live map lives in State.map, seeded from Cart::map(); mset writes it, cart keeps the pristine copy. Persists across frames, replays deterministically with zero special handling (verified two ways: two consoles 60 frames identical fb, and console-agent --screen-text twice byte-identical).\n\nBACK-COMPAT: no __map__ => all-zero map; map() draws nothing, mget 0, mset works. No golden changed. ONE pre-existing test touched: cart_parse::unknown_sections_are_preserved_not_rejected used __map__ as its example unknown section — swapped to __save__.\n\nFILES: crates/console-core/src/{gfx,cart,api,state,lib}.rs, tests/map.rs (new, 29 tests), tests/cart_parse.rs (1 line), SPEC.md, skills/build-cart/SKILL.md.\n\ncargo test --workspace green (355 tests, 29 new). clippy --all-targets clean.\n\nWATCH OUT: 'cargo fmt --all' rewrites ~20 unrelated files — the repo predates this rustfmt version. I stashed that noise back out; my diff touches only the files above. (bn-cp0 left an identical stash, so this bites everyone; might be worth pinning a rustfmt version.) api.rs/state.rs diffs kept surgical for the concurrent audio worker.\n\nINTEGRATION: engine.js needs a rebuild for map/mget/mset to ship in packed HTML — the new globals are registered in console-core so console-web picks them up automatically, but the committed web/engine.js is stale until rebuilt. No C ABI change needed. Map authoring/preview tooling stays out of scope here (bn-2tf)."}	blake3:pFwMRWf6nUpbut3MfKWLiklq6FhowEHHuZlxiBk2R4g
1785725851577598	console-w-34g	itc:v3:AWLJM-ckySZnPEAAAAAAQdW-6tVt3gAAAAEwAw		item.comment	bn-34g	{"body":"Echo bus core landed in .maw/workspaces/bn-34g: Echo{delay(frames 1-60),feedback(0-8, max 7/8),level(0-8)} + per-inst echo=<0-8> send, one-pole 4800Hz LP inside the feedback loop, fixed 44100-sample boxed delay line. All 3 existing goldens pass untouched (echo off = legacy statement). Next: soundtest ECHO entry + docs."}	blake3:ohj59Zy_N_UKAfXXs2pNDJQuBrk1lXxb0eIQBRL56iY
1785725866613841	console-dev	itc:v3:AWLmTP-ZOTJklAAAAAAAQe1v-11rVAAAAAEuWA		item.move	bn-153	{"state":"done"}	blake3:VOM6hiQ15ip8lWqYVDt-bsR12Aygj40hcaoulNDJXlw
1785725876024130	console-dev	itc:v3:AWLmTP-ZOTJklAAAAAAAQe1v-11rVAAAAAEuWQ		item.create	bn-1qo	{"description":"Both bn-cp0 and bn-153 workers had to stash out ~900-line formatting churn because the tree predates the locally installed rustfmt. Options: pin a rustfmt toolchain in rust-toolchain.toml, commit one blanket cargo fmt pass, or add a just fmt scoped to changed files. Decide and apply.","kind":"task","title":"Pin rustfmt / add scoped fmt task — local rustfmt rewrites ~20 unrelated files"}	blake3:P-wsMSDUkB2n7OYDY9n-AGjxQCjVGHV_FjHNwxDETJc
