1785728196458731	console-w-2tf	itc:v3:AWLJMn_kySfmUAAAAAAAQdWv_Wq_aAAAAAEtAg		item.assign	bn-2tf	{"action":"assign","agent":"console-w-2tf"}	blake3:7Bt5My5yKMYRMx6qU5gZwKDylUKkjRB-vA2-FGsIN-M
1785728208371957	console-w-3hy	itc:v3:AWLPyczMkk5PxAAAAAAAQd-u21V1-AAAAAEuAw		item.comment	bn-3hy	{"body":"rshift(y, dx) landed in workspace bn-3hy (commit b8a1ab5), ready for merge.\n\nWRAP RULE: dx is reduced with a Euclidean remainder mod SCREEN_W (144) and stored as 0..=143 rightward pixels; pixel at column x lands at (x + dx) mod 144. Every argument is legal: -1 == 143, dx == dx +/- 144n, rshift(y, 144) stores 0 (identity). Fractional dx floored like every coord; y outside 0..255 is a no-op. Wrap, not clip, so sine sweeps are seamless.\n\nAPI: write-only. rshift() clears the whole table; rshift(y) is rshift(y, 0) and clears one line; rshift(y, dx) sets one. No getter in Lua; Rust hosts get DrawState::rshift(y)/rshift_table()/rshift_active().\n\nPIPELINE: _draw() -> mosaic -> rshift -> present (display palette at scanout). Order rationale: mosaic pixelates the finished frame first, rshift then displaces already-pixelated scanlines, so a shift can never split a mosaic block into partial halves and water-over-mosaic reads right. Applied to the presented snapshot in Console::sync_framebuffer; the pristine draw buffer, pget and next-frame drawing are untouched, so nothing compounds. Table is draw state: persists across frames, part of console state, included in DrawState equality/determinism.\n\nBACK-COMPAT: all-zero table (the default) is detected in O(1) via a nonzero-line counter, and sync_framebuffer skips the copy and the pass entirely, so untouched carts get bit-identical framebuffers. All pre-existing tests/goldens pass unmodified.\n\nFILES: crates/console-core/src/gfx.rs (ShiftTable type, DrawState fields + set_rshift/reset_rshift/rshift/rshift_table/rshift_active, apply_rshift via in-place slice::rotate_right - no allocation), src/api.rs (+18 lines, the rshift binding only), src/lib.rs (ShiftTable export + sync_framebuffer order), tests/effects.rs (11 new tests + back-compat/determinism extensions, 45 pass), SPEC.md (API row, draw-state block, frame-pipeline section, host surfaces), skills/build-cart/SKILL.md (API line + raster-effect idioms: water sine sweep, parallax bands, bottom-half reflection), README.md (draw-state list).\n\nTESTS: cargo test --workspace green in the workspace; cargo clippy -p console-core --all-targets clean. cargo fmt touched only my new lines (the repo at large is not fmt-clean under rustfmt 1.9.0 - 235 pre-existing hunks on trunk - so I did not reformat anything else).\n\nPERF: 3600 frames at release, agent 'run': baseline 0.03s, static shift table on every line 0.03s (the rotate pass is below noise, ~36KB of memmove/frame), full Lua sine sweep 0.13s (~28us/frame, and that is the 256 Lua calls + trig, not the pass).\n\nINTEGRATION: engine rebuild required (console-core changed); no host code changes - console-agent/console-web/web shell already present Console::framebuffer(), which folds both post-effects."}	blake3:AZ_OcOomHLzf5yDzLf4XAH7OKkvsJRFK3tBnbnn83ZE
